# Repowise ignore file — same exclusions as .repowise/config.yaml exclude_patterns.
# Fixture/test workspaces and non-production folders are excluded so code-health
# scores, dead-code findings, and MCP results reflect production code only.
# Mirrors .codacy.yaml exclusions and .repowise/bot.yaml ignore_paths.
workspaces-bad/
workspaces-good/
crates/*/tests/
scripts/
tools/
log/
target/
*.md

# Rust binary entry points (fn main, declared in Cargo.toml [[bin]]).
# repowise flags them as unreachable because they are never imported —
# that is their nature, not dead code (known repowise false positive).
crates/root_cli_main_entry.rs
crates/root_mcp_main_entry.rs
crates/root_tui_main_entry.rs

# AES module barrels (pure `pub mod` / `pub use` re-exports — no logic).
# repowise flags the shared re-export pattern as duplication across every
# module's mod.rs/lib.rs; that is intrinsic to the AES layered architecture,
# not removable duplication (merging would break the 327 dependents).
# Known repowise false positive — exclude from health scoring.
# Only verified-pure barrels are excluded; lib.rs carrying real logic is
# re-included below so its health is still scored. build.rs is NOT excluded
# (build scripts contain real logic).
**/mod.rs
**/lib.rs
!crates/external-lint/src/lib.rs

